# Wi-Fi firmware. The onboard radio on Pi 3B/3B+/4B/CM4 is Broadcom/Cypress
# (BCM43438 on the 3B, BCM43455/CYW43455 on 3B+/4/CM4), so firmware-brcm80211
# is mandatory. Onboard Bluetooth firmware comes from bluez-firmware, pulled in
# by pi-bluetooth, and is unaffected by what is dropped here.
#
# Dropped:
#   firmware-atheros  (38 MB) - nearly all of it is ath10k/ath11k firmware and
#     board files for PCIe cards, and a Pi 3/4 has no PCIe slot. Only ath9k_htc
#     USB dongles (e.g. TP-Link TL-WN722N v1) lose support.
#   firmware-libertas (3.6 MB) - Marvell Libertas. No Pi uses it and the USB
#     dongles that did are long obsolete.
#
# Kept firmware-realtek + firmware-misc-nonfree (8.5 MB combined): Realtek and
# Ralink/MediaTek are the two most common chipsets in the cheap USB Wi-Fi
# dongles field users plug in -- not worth the support calls to save 8 MB.
firmware-brcm80211 firmware-misc-nonfree firmware-realtek
